experience.description:
Taxation, Audit, Consulting, Accounting
Tools and programs applied: SAP, Quick Book, Thomas Reuters ACS 
- Preparation and review of financial statements for US clients on a quarterly and annual basis;
- Preparation and filing of individual's (form 1040) and corporate tax returns (forms 1120, the 1120S and 1065), payroll reports and sales tax returns  for US clients
- Preparation and submission of Sales and Use Tax returns for the client from the Fortune 500 list all over the USA;

Main engagements:
- End to end coordination and execution of annual financial statement audits, from signing the LoE to issuance of the audit opinion, bridge/conversion file (US GAAP to Stat) review and ownership of the Stat balances after adjustments for the entities across the EMEA region;
- Assess the differences in the accounting treatment of transactions between US GAAP and local GAAP, making sure that the US and local books are aligned;
- Leading projects, e.g., organize, standardize, plan transition to an accounting team within EMEA focused on Stat financial reporting;
- Coordination and alignment with central and local teams of external providers (accountants, auditors) to implement process improvements, standardize procedures and deliverables and set out timelines;
- Liaise efficiently with multiple internal stakeholders, e.g. tax department, legal, treasury, payroll etc to build up processes and efficiently streamline the information flow;
- Handling of complex fillings following local regulations such as financial statements on a basis other than going concern;
- Help the Stat team reach its overall goals, provide guidance to accountants, onboard new joiners;
- Tracking of the filing progress as per the EMEA scheduling.

Main engagements:
- Completion of the full monthly closing process for various entities within EMEA; - Review and perform variance analysis on balance sheet and profit and loss accounts during the closing procedures, document the account balances after the close process is completed; - Collect, compile, verify, and analyze financial information and review/prepare reports such as financial statements or regulatory filings such as VAT and CIT declarations;
- Coordinating multiple external providers, e.g., local accountants, tax consultants, lawyers etc;
- End to end coordination of annual financial statement audits, from signing the LoE to issuance of the audit opinion, bridge/conversion file (US GAAP to Stat) review and ownership of the Stat balances after adjustments.

Main engagements:
- Preparation and/or review of the conversion from management GAAP (US GAAP, IFRS) to local GAAP for EMEA countries;
- Preparation and/or review of financial statements for EMEA countries (in local language and English);
- Coordination and review of local CIT returns for countries across the EMEA region; 
- Wide responsibility in terms of day-to day interactions with clients in an international environment;
- Assistance to the managing team with the coordination of the delivery of accounting and tax services to an international client portfolio;
-Support of statutory and tax audits.

Main engagements:
- Day-to-day and year-end bookkeeping services; 
- Drawing-up financial statements according to Greek GAAP & IFRS;
- Preparing the monthly and quarterly accounting reporting (Trial Balance, Cash Flow and Projection reporting under Greek and  US accounts);
- Preparing and filing the corporate income tax, withholding taxes and VAT returns;
- Handling of complex tax and accounting tasks such as M&A’s, dissolution and liquidation of legal entities, implications of cross border transactions;
- Providing support during tax  or financial audits/inspections;
- Identifying and reporting possible problems as regards client procedures to the supervising team in a professional and  proactive manner; 
- Being in constant direct relation with clients worldwide and third parties (administration, banks, clients’ associates);
- Guidance of more junior team members-mainly interns.

